1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,800
This is the shipped rex-tg Mini App in its phone layout,
served by its Go handler.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:12,000
It uses isolated local fixtures. No live Telegram account,
bot, Rex pane, or agent is connected.

3
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:18,500
Agents shows linked sessions, status, folders, and current tasks.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:25,160
Expand a card to open its topic, screen, files, or changes,
or rename or unlink the session.

5
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:29,500
Topics separates live and stopped conversations.

6
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:37,780
New agent lets you choose pi, Claude Code, or Codex,
then select a project folder. This tour stops before starting anything.

7
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:42,700
Screen uses the bundled xterm component to render pane output.

8
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:45,100
Pause refresh or fit the output to the viewport.

9
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,840
No terminal input is sent during this tour.

10
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:52,800
Files browses the project and opens Markdown or source.

11
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,510
Reads stay inside the selected project folder.

12
00:00:57,010 --> 00:00:59,600
Changes compares uncommitted work and branch history.

13
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,140
Open a file to inspect the Git diff.

14
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:08,200
Annotate loads answers for this topic. Tap a passage
to add a note, then review it.

15
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:12,740
This demo stores only a local draft;
it sends nothing to an agent.

16
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:21,030
This is rex-tg's real Mini App with sample data.
The README covers live setup, security, and known limits.
